This doc is the **prose front-door** to the `.add/ai/` foundation: it carries the
*identity*, the *bar*, and the *budget* a human owns, then points at the named-set
artifacts (`eval-set.jsonl` · `rubric.json` · `eval-spec.json` · `io-contract.json` ·
`fallback.md` · `monitor.json`) the AI builds against and the eval gate scores.

## Identity

The AI component's identity is **human-owned** — set it here at specify; never let the
AI invent the task. Fill each prompt with your real values, then delete the comment.

- **Component** — <!-- the one AI feature this doc binds, e.g. "support-reply drafter" -->
- **Task type** — <!-- generation | rag | agent — decides which eval-spec blocks are required -->
- **What it hires the model to do** — <!-- one line: the job, in the user's terms -->

## Success metric

The bar is **human-owned** — the engine measures the recorded score, it never invents
the metric or sets the threshold. Tie it to business impact, not to a vanity number.

- **Business impact** — <!-- the outcome that pays for this component, e.g. "deflect 30% of tickets" -->
- **Top-line quality metric** — <!-- the single primary metric the verify gate reads (names eval-spec.json primary_metric) -->
- **Threshold to ship** — <!-- the pass bar; below this returns to Build, never lower it (names eval-spec.json threshold) -->
- **Baseline to beat** — <!-- majority | random | heuristic | human | prior-model + its score; quality > baseline or it is non-evidence -->

## Criteria

The four buckets every AI component is scored on — each names the `rubric.json`
criterion that measures it. Fill each prompt; a missing bucket goes red.

- **Capability** — <!-- can it do the task at all? names the rubric criterion -->
- **Generation faithfulness** — <!-- is the output grounded / non-hallucinated? names the rubric criterion -->
- **Instruction following** — <!-- does it honor format + constraints? names the rubric criterion -->
- **Cost / latency** — <!-- is each call inside budget? names the rubric criterion -->

## Model pin

The model-under-test is **pinned** — a recorded score is only reproducible when the run
is fixed. Pin it here and mirror it into `MODEL_REGISTRY.md`; a change is a change
request, not a silent edit.

- **Model + version** — <!-- the model id and version the score is earned against -->
- **Temperature** — <!-- the sampling temperature; judges pin temperature = 0 -->
- **Seed** — <!-- the fixed seed; report variance over ≥ 2 samples, never one -->
- **Prompt / template version** — <!-- the prompt or template version, so the score is rebuildable -->

## Method ladder

The **prompt → RAG → finetune** ladder is the default — the cheapest adaptation that
works. An escalation must be earned; record the cheaper rungs shown exhausted.

- **Chosen rung** — <!-- prompt | rag | finetune -->
- **Why the cheaper rungs were exhausted** — <!-- what prompting/RAG was tried first and where it fell short; a finetune is a flagged decision the human approves -->

## Eval strategy

The eval contract is the AI analog of the red suite — frozen before build, never
weakened. It points at the `.add/ai/` set the validators lint.

- **Eval set** — <!-- the held-out distribution scored against; names eval-set.jsonl (≥ 1 case, ≥ 10 recommended) -->
- **Disjoint split** — <!-- train / val / test row counts + the split key; the test split is sacred, never tuned on -->
- **Judge pin** — <!-- if any dimension is judge-scored: judge model + version + temperature 0 + seed + samples ≥ 2, judge ≠ model-under-test -->
- **Lineage** — <!-- the eval-set content hash + model/data version the verify gate records (mirrored in eval-spec.json + MODEL_REGISTRY.md) -->

## Guardrails

The safety floor is **non-negotiable** — a guardrail eval finding is a HARD-STOP, never
auto-passed. Declare the classes here; wire each to a fallback line in `fallback.md`.

- **Guardrail classes** — <!-- prompt-injection · indirect-injection · PII · toxicity · jailbreak · refusal -->
- **PII / external-API boundary** — <!-- what must never leave to an external model -->
- **Trip behavior** — <!-- the safe path each tripped guardrail takes (names a fallback.md line) -->

## Budget

Cost and latency are **first-class acceptance constraints** — the verify eval run
measures them; an over-budget build fails even when quality passes.

- **Latency envelope** — <!-- p50 / p90 / p99 ceilings the eval run measures (mirrored in io-contract.json budget) -->
- **Cost per request** — <!-- the per-call cost ceiling -->

## Data provenance

Where the eval and any training data come from — the leakage and contamination guard.

- **Data sources** — <!-- where eval-set.jsonl cases originate; what licence / consent covers them -->
- **Train-only transforms** — <!-- any scaler/vocab/encoder fit on train only, never test (names io-contract.json train_only_transforms) -->
- **Contamination check** — <!-- confirm no eval case appears in a finetune/training set — a model scored on its own training data is non-evidence -->

## I/O contract

The pinned I/O boundary — the same contract both sides, output-schema-validated before
use. Points at `io-contract.json`.

- **Request / response schema** — <!-- the pinned request + response schema the boundary validates (names io-contract.json) -->
- **Reader policy** — <!-- lenient: unknown fields tolerated + preserved; a strict-reject needs a documented reason -->
- **Idempotency / retry** — <!-- the idempotency key or no-side-effect assertion + the bounded retry/backoff -->
- **Schema-invalid output** — <!-- a non-conforming output takes the fallback path and never propagates -->

## Fallback

A probabilistic system without a declared fallback is unsafe by construction — every
failure mode names a concrete safe path. Points at `fallback.md`.

- **Per-failure safe state** — <!-- timeout · error · low-confidence · schema-invalid · guardrail-trip (+ empty-retrieval for RAG / tool-failure for agent), each a cached/default/cheaper-model/human-in-loop/hard-deny path — never crash/hang -->
- **Timeout + bound** — <!-- the timeout_ms + bounded retry / circuit-breaker (names fallback.md ## Limits) -->

## Observe / monitor

The Observe-phase online-eval + drift artifact — re-run a sample of the eval set against
production, record the offline-vs-online delta. Points at `monitor.json`.

- **Live signals** — <!-- quality/safety drift vs the frozen score · latency p50/p90/p99 · cost/request · ≥ 1 implicit user-feedback signal (names monitor.json signals) -->
- **Drift baseline** — <!-- the baseline metric + score + alert threshold the live delta is measured against -->
- **Drift → reopen** — <!-- drift below the frozen threshold surfaces as a spec delta / reopen at Specify — never a silent regression -->

## Foundation

The named-set artifacts the validators lint and the eval gate scores — live under
`.add/ai/`; author them at the contract freeze, then never weaken them:

- **Eval set** — `ai/eval-set.jsonl` · the frozen, held-out cases (one JSON object per
  line); the AI analog of the red suite. Disjoint train/val/test split; the test split
  is sacred.
- **Rubric** — `ai/rubric.json` · the scored acceptance rubric (the four buckets +
  per-criterion thresholds) the verify gate reads.
- **Eval spec** — `ai/eval-spec.json` · the reproducible run config + the pre-registered
  gate (primary metric + threshold + baseline + disjoint split + pinned judge +
  eval-set hash).
- **I/O contract** — `ai/io-contract.json` · the pinned model id(s), request/response
  schema, guardrails, idempotency/retry, and budget — validated at the boundary.
- **Fallback** — `ai/fallback.md` · the per-failure-mode safe state + the timeout /
  bounded-retry limits.
- **Monitor** — `ai/monitor.json` · the Observe-phase online-eval + drift signals, the
  drift baseline, and the alert policy.

`add.py check` lints this named set in place — a missing / malformed / leaky /
unthresholded artifact goes red with a named code; it is silent when there is no
`ai/` set. The frozen eval set + thresholds are hashed into the tamper-tripwire:
lowering a threshold, mutating a frozen test row, or weakening the rubric is a
`build_tampered` HARD-STOP, never launderable through RISK-ACCEPTED.

## Gate

For a task-kind `ai`, the verify gate reads the **eval score, not a green unit test**:
it PASSES only when measured-score ≥ the frozen threshold **AND** > baseline **AND** the
lineage (eval-set hash + model/data version) is recorded. A below-threshold score
returns to Build — never lower the threshold, never trim the eval set. A safety /
guardrail finding and any leakage finding are HARD-STOP.
